  "description": "ABUSIVE-DYNAMICS V1 -- EVIDENTIARY VISIBILITY (block 364000). Does a discrete, victim-independent incident trace protect credibility a purely diffuse pattern cannot earn? (ABUSIVE_RELATIONSHIPS_VISIBILITY_SCOPING.md Part E, V1). Composes N1's own dyad (snap_frustration block 242000 + arousal_window_coreg block 239000, BOTH UNMODIFIED) via a byte-identical restatement of N1's own n1_victim_entrainment rule (v1_victim_entrainment) -- N1's own seed (abusive_n1_credibility_loop) is READ for this rule's SHAPE, never depended on or edited, matching R3's own convention against R2. v1_network_credibility_incident_aware extends N1's own credibility-comparison rule SHAPE by exactly one new discount term: cred_abuser = charm_weight*seen_charm - incident_discount_weight*seen_incident (a NEW, discrete, victim-independent observable -- direct evidence AGAINST the abuser's conduct, deliberately wired to discount the ABUSER's credibility term rather than boost the VICTIM's claim term -- conflating 'there is evidence of what he did' with 'she is more believable' would smuggle back the exact victim-credibility framing this line dissolves). cred_victim is UNCHANGED from N1's own formula (claim_weight*seen_victim_claim - instability_discount_weight*seen_victim_unstable). ONE shared rule serves BOTH of V1's arms (INCIDENT_VISIBLE / INCIDENT_INVISIBLE) -- the only difference between arms is whether the world adapter ever delivers a nonzero seen_incident, mechanically, under the SAME counter-DELTA-observer idiom R3's own r3_prior_track_narrow/_widen already established (wot.narrow_count > wot.pn_last_narrow) -- never a read of the transient in_snap/snapped flags (N1's own Sec. 2.1 finding). seen_charm is delivered as a mechanical constant (+=1.0/tick) rather than restating N1's own n1_abuser_stated_charm rule, because that rule, under deception_on=1 (fixed ON in every one of N1's own arms), always evaluates to stated_charm=1.0 unconditionally -- a structural constant at V1's own single-dyad operating point, reproduced byte-identically without the extra rule. v1_network_credibility_incident_aware's own `where` is a trivially-true Eq(1.0,1.0) (matching bigville_loud_comm.json's lo_choose_loudness idiom), not `where: None` -- an engine finding surfaced while building this rule: a null-where rule fires on the first full run_rules() pass but is not re-triggered by the engine's incremental dirty-tracking on a subsequent attribute change (confirmed directly against the real graph). NO reward/punishment anywhere. NO Rust, NO new Term (Plus/Minus/Times/Attr/Var/Lit/Eq/Lt/And only, all already used by snap_frustration/arousal_window_coreg/abusive_n1_credibility_loop). self_load_only, default-OFF.",
  "microtheory": {
    "name": "evidentiary_visibility",
    "description": "A network node's belief tracks only what evidence reaches it. The credibility-asymmetry loop N1 already validated does not change; what changes is whether ONE more channel of evidence -- a discrete, victim-independent trace of the abuser's own conduct -- ever reaches the network at all. The loop's cruelty in the diffuse-only case is not that the network judges unfairly; it is that a purely diffuse pattern of harm structurally produces no evidence of the kind an incident-shaped credibility rule can act on."
  },
